## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates translating CKNE into batch ETL resource control and SLA guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource mapping for batch jobs
- Minute-based rebalancing with fairness bounds
- Per-tenant queues, batching, and backpressure
- Observability: latency, throughput, CKNE drift

## Code Example
```javascript
function clamp(v, min, max){ return Math.max(min, Math.min(max, v)); }
function computeParams(ckne, base=1, alpha=2, minWindow=5, maxWindow=60, beta=0.5){
  const c = clamp(Math.round(base + alpha*ckne), 1, 8);
  const w = clamp(Math.round(minWindow + beta*(maxWindow-minWindow)*ckne), minWindow, maxWindow);
  return {concurrency:c, batchWindow:w};
}
```

